Test job to run a MC simulation for a solute with GB/SA
hydration. To run here, enter

For Linux/Unix:
csh gbcmd >& log &
For Windows:
gb

This uses gbzmat as the Z-matrix for the solute(s).

To run in any directory for a Z-matrix, zmat.z, use
xMCGB zmat

gbout contains the output for 1,2-dichloroethane.
gasout is the corresponding output for DCE in the gas phase
without the GB/SA solvation (using the MCgas test job).

gbcmd like gascmd performs 1M configurations of equilibration 
and 2 M configurations of averaging.
Time required:
170 sec with GB/SA
 92 sec without GB/SA
on a 2.4 GHz Pentium
